{"analysis_output_files": 52, "charts": [{"alt": "House 2026: no clear candidate-type advantage. House 2026 associations adjust for presidential lean and lean squared; the incumbency model additionally controls Republican incumbency. All other traits compare verified Democratic incumbents. One share point equals two D-minus-R margin points. Senate record comparisons have only nine candidates. A held fit is not zero.", "caption": "House 2026 associations adjust for presidential lean and lean squared; the incumbency model additionally controls Republican incumbency. All other traits compare verified Democratic incumbents. One share point equals two D-minus-R margin points. Senate record comparisons have only nine candidates. A held fit is not zero.", "data": "plot-data/house-characteristics.csv", "files": {"marginoferror": {"background": "#F2EFE7", "height": 1500, "png": "marginoferror/house-characteristics.png", "svg": "marginoferror/house-characteristics.svg", "width": 2360}, "substack": {"background": "#F7F5F0", "height": 1500, "png": "substack/house-characteristics.png", "svg": "substack/house-characteristics.svg", "width": 2360}}, "id": "house-characteristics", "plotted_records": 6, "title": "House 2026: no clear candidate-type advantage"}, {"alt": "House: 2026 alongside five earlier elections. House annual associations for 2016, 2018, 2020, 2022, 2024 and 2026. The 2026 fits are reused unchanged; earlier years are exploratory annual fits with the same lean/lean-squared controls and pre-election feature rules. Except incumbency, traits compare verified Democratic incumbents. Midterms use a lagged presidential benchmark; presidential years use a same-year benchmark. Cohorts, maps and record coverage differ. These are not paired-candidate changes, a formal test of changes between years, or a correction across all historical comparisons. Held fits are not zero.", "caption": "House annual associations for 2016, 2018, 2020, 2022, 2024 and 2026. The 2026 fits are reused unchanged; earlier years are exploratory annual fits with the same lean/lean-squared controls and pre-election feature rules. Except incumbency, traits compare verified Democratic incumbents. Midterms use a lagged presidential benchmark; presidential years use a same-year benchmark. Cohorts, maps and record coverage differ. These are not paired-candidate changes, a formal test of changes between years, or a correction across all historical comparisons. Held fits are not zero.", "data": "plot-data/house-history.csv", "files": {"marginoferror": {"background": "#F2EFE7", "height": 2120, "png": "marginoferror/house-history.png", "svg": "marginoferror/house-history.svg", "width": 2360}, "substack": {"background": "#F7F5F0", "height": 2120, "png": "substack/house-history.png", "svg": "substack/house-history.svg", "width": 2360}}, "id": "house-history", "plotted_records": 36, "title": "House: 2026 alongside five earlier elections"}, {"alt": "Senate 2026: no clear candidate-type advantage. Senate 2026 associations adjust for presidential lean and lean squared; the incumbency model additionally controls Republican incumbency. All other traits compare verified Democratic incumbents. One share point equals two D-minus-R margin points. Senate record comparisons have only nine candidates. A held fit is not zero.", "caption": "Senate 2026 associations adjust for presidential lean and lean squared; the incumbency model additionally controls Republican incumbency. All other traits compare verified Democratic incumbents. One share point equals two D-minus-R margin points. Senate record comparisons have only nine candidates. A held fit is not zero.", "data": "plot-data/senate-characteristics.csv", "files": {"marginoferror": {"background": "#F2EFE7", "height": 1500, "png": "marginoferror/senate-characteristics.png", "svg": "marginoferror/senate-characteristics.svg", "width": 2360}, "substack": {"background": "#F7F5F0", "height": 1500, "png": "substack/senate-characteristics.png", "svg": "substack/senate-characteristics.svg", "width": 2360}}, "id": "senate-characteristics", "plotted_records": 6, "title": "Senate 2026: no clear candidate-type advantage"}, {"alt": "Senate: 2026 alongside five earlier elections. Senate annual associations for 2016, 2018, 2020, 2022, 2024 and 2026. The 2026 fits are reused unchanged; earlier years are exploratory annual fits with the same lean/lean-squared controls and pre-election feature rules. Except incumbency, traits compare verified Democratic incumbents. Midterms use a lagged presidential benchmark; presidential years use a same-year benchmark. Cohorts, maps and record coverage differ. These are not paired-candidate changes, a formal test of changes between years, or a correction across all historical comparisons. Held fits are not zero.", "caption": "Senate annual associations for 2016, 2018, 2020, 2022, 2024 and 2026. The 2026 fits are reused unchanged; earlier years are exploratory annual fits with the same lean/lean-squared controls and pre-election feature rules. Except incumbency, traits compare verified Democratic incumbents. Midterms use a lagged presidential benchmark; presidential years use a same-year benchmark. Cohorts, maps and record coverage differ. These are not paired-candidate changes, a formal test of changes between years, or a correction across all historical comparisons. Held fits are not zero.", "data": "plot-data/senate-history.csv", "files": {"marginoferror": {"background": "#F2EFE7", "height": 2120, "png": "marginoferror/senate-history.png", "svg": "marginoferror/senate-history.svg", "width": 2360}, "substack": {"background": "#F7F5F0", "height": 2120, "png": "substack/senate-history.png", "svg": "substack/senate-history.svg", "width": 2360}}, "id": "senate-history", "plotted_records": 36, "title": "Senate: 2026 alongside five earlier elections"}, {"alt": "Voting records give no decisive 2026 signal. Each point is a candidate's presidential-benchmark gap after subtracting the saved model's lean-control contribution relative to its sample mean. Lines hold those controls at their sample means. Each panel retains its exact saved sample. Neither slope passes the primary six-test Holm correction.", "caption": "Each point is a candidate's presidential-benchmark gap after subtracting the saved model's lean-control contribution relative to its sample mean. Lines hold those controls at their sample means. Each panel retains its exact saved sample. Neither slope passes the primary six-test Holm correction.", "data": "plot-data/house-voting-records.csv", "files": {"marginoferror": {"background": "#F2EFE7", "height": 1500, "png": "marginoferror/house-voting-records.png", "svg": "marginoferror/house-voting-records.svg", "width": 2360}, "substack": {"background": "#F7F5F0", "height": 1500, "png": "substack/house-voting-records.png", "svg": "substack/house-voting-records.svg", "width": 2360}}, "id": "house-voting-records", "plotted_records": 461, "title": "Voting records give no decisive 2026 signal"}, {"alt": "Identity comparisons remain inconclusive in 2026. Selected documented Democratic incumbents only, on compatible district maps. The race comparison is Asian/Pacific Islander versus Black, not White versus minority or all nominees. There is no qualified atheist comparison. ACS controls describe residents, not voters; compatible 2026 district religious composition is unavailable. The nominal Muslim interval excludes zero but does not survive multiplicity correction.", "caption": "Selected documented Democratic incumbents only, on compatible district maps. The race comparison is Asian/Pacific Islander versus Black, not White versus minority or all nominees. There is no qualified atheist comparison. ACS controls describe residents, not voters; compatible 2026 district religious composition is unavailable. The nominal Muslim interval excludes zero but does not survive multiplicity correction.", "data": "plot-data/identity-comparisons.csv", "files": {"marginoferror": {"background": "#F2EFE7", "height": 1500, "png": "marginoferror/identity-comparisons.png", "svg": "marginoferror/identity-comparisons.svg", "width": 2360}, "substack": {"background": "#F7F5F0", "height": 1500, "png": "substack/identity-comparisons.png", "svg": "substack/identity-comparisons.svg", "width": 2360}}, "id": "identity-comparisons", "plotted_records": 4, "title": "Identity comparisons remain inconclusive in 2026"}, {"alt": "Missing identity evidence limits the 2026 comparison. All religion and race categories are shown, including zeros. Counts are 2026 candidate observations, not estimates of Congress's overall composition. Positive Historian group lists do not identify everyone outside those groups. Unknown Hispanic origin never supplies a non-Hispanic comparison group.", "caption": "All religion and race categories are shown, including zeros. Counts are 2026 candidate observations, not estimates of Congress's overall composition. Positive Historian group lists do not identify everyone outside those groups. Unknown Hispanic origin never supplies a non-Hispanic comparison group.", "data": "plot-data/identity-coverage.csv", "files": {"marginoferror": {"background": "#F2EFE7", "height": 1900, "png": "marginoferror/identity-coverage.png", "svg": "marginoferror/identity-coverage.svg", "width": 2360}, "substack": {"background": "#F7F5F0", "height": 1900, "png": "substack/identity-coverage.png", "svg": "substack/identity-coverage.svg", "width": 2360}}, "id": "identity-coverage", "plotted_records": 30, "title": "Missing identity evidence limits the 2026 comparison"}, {"alt": "Trait records add little predictive lift for 2026. Each feature is compared with a baseline on its own identical held-out candidates, not on a common sample across features. House samples range from 130 to 349; Senate samples from 8 to 23. Birth in state is exploratory. Small error differences are not a statistical test that one nominee type is better.", "caption": "Each feature is compared with a baseline on its own identical held-out candidates, not on a common sample across features. House samples range from 130 to 349; Senate samples from 8 to 23. Birth in state is exploratory. Small error differences are not a statistical test that one nominee type is better.", "data": "plot-data/predictive-lift.csv", "files": {"marginoferror": {"background": "#F2EFE7", "height": 1500, "png": "marginoferror/predictive-lift.png", "svg": "marginoferror/predictive-lift.svg", "width": 2360}, "substack": {"background": "#F7F5F0", "height": 1500, "png": "substack/predictive-lift.png", "svg": "substack/predictive-lift.svg", "width": 2360}}, "id": "predictive-lift", "plotted_records": 14, "title": "Trait records add little predictive lift for 2026"}, {"alt": "2026: partisan geography sets the starting point. All 408 eligible House and 29 Senate comparisons, including unresolved incumbency. This is a descriptive benchmark comparison, not a causal model or evidence that two elections had identical electorates. House benchmarks use 2026 district maps; unqualified rounds and absent major-party nominees remain outside the plot.", "caption": "All 408 eligible House and 29 Senate comparisons, including unresolved incumbency. This is a descriptive benchmark comparison, not a causal model or evidence that two elections had identical electorates. House benchmarks use 2026 district maps; unqualified rounds and absent major-party nominees remain outside the plot.", "data": "plot-data/partisan-geography.csv", "files": {"marginoferror": {"background": "#F2EFE7", "height": 1500, "png": "marginoferror/partisan-geography.png", "svg": "marginoferror/partisan-geography.svg", "width": 2360}, "substack": {"background": "#F7F5F0", "height": 1500, "png": "substack/partisan-geography.png", "svg": "substack/partisan-geography.svg", "width": 2360}}, "id": "partisan-geography", "plotted_records": 437, "title": "2026: partisan geography sets the starting point"}], "comparison_scope": "Expl